{%- comment -%}
  Casa Judge.me Rating Badge

  Renders the Judge.me preview badge using the server-side metafield
  pattern from Judge.me's official OS 2.0 install docs:
  https://judge.me/help/en/articles/8263435

  The metafield {{ product.metafields.judgeme.badge }} contains the
  pre-rendered stars + count HTML. No AJAX reload required — Liquid
  prints it server-side. data-auto-install='false' tells Judge.me's
  loader to leave it alone (the metafield already filled it).

  Parameters:
  - product: The product object (required)
  - link: Optional boolean (default false). Judge.me bakes
    role='button' + tabindex='0' into its stars span so the stars act
    as a "scroll to the reviews widget" control. Keep that ONLY where a
    reviews widget lives on the same page — the PDP buy-box, which
    passes link: true.

    Default (every card surface: product cards, cart drawer, comparison
    table, lookbook) is PRESENTATIONAL: the stars are swapped to
    role='img' + tabindex='-1'. On those surfaces the whole card is
    already an <a> to the PDP, so Judge.me's focusable "button" nested
    inside that link is a dead keyboard tab stop (one per card) and an
    axe `nested-interactive` (WCAG 2.2 AA 4.1.2) violation. role='img'
    keeps the existing aria-label="N stars" as the text alternative —
    the same "a rating is a labelled image" pattern used by
    blocks/mini-reviews.liquid. Pairs with the pointer-events:none card
    rule in assets/casa-base.css (that kills the mouse affordance; this
    kills the keyboard/AT affordance).

  Prerequisites:
  - Judge.me App Embed enabled in theme editor (Online Store > Themes
    > Edit theme > App embeds > Judge.me)
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if product != blank -%}
  <div
    class="jdgm-widget jdgm-preview-badge"
    data-id="{{ product.id }}"
    data-auto-install="false"
  >
    {%- if link -%}
      {{ product.metafields.judgeme.badge }}
    {%- else -%}
      {{ product.metafields.judgeme.badge | replace: "role='button'", "role='img'" | replace: "tabindex='0'", "tabindex='-1'" }}
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
